ail): submission prevented by browser validation. Invalid fields identified to user through browser's built-in validation UI.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid salary range accepted without validation.\", \"actual\": \"Job \\\"Test Job\\\" was posted successfully with minimum salary $200k and maximum salary $100k (min > max). The salary values should be validated so minimum is not greater than maximum. Validation should produce clear feedback before allowing publication. Job was accepted and posted displaying invalid range \\\"$200k - $100k\\\".\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Duplicate applications not prevented.\", \"actual\": \"Successfully submitted a second application for Senior Frontend Developer using duplicate email alex.j@email.com (which already had an application on that job). Application count increased from 2 to 3, confirming duplicate was accepted. System should have prevented this and displayed error message to user.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Successfully submitted application for John Smith (john.smith@test.com, 555-1234) appears exactly once under Senior Backend Developer job in employer dashboard with all submitted information: name, email, phone, message, and submission date (Yesterday).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tested with Industry filter and keyword search. Industry filter for Technology: 9 jobs → 3 jobs with immediate count update to \\\"Showing 3 jobs\\\". Keyword search for \\\"Python\\\": 9 jobs → 2 jobs with immediate count update. Clearing filters: 3 jobs → 9 jobs with \\\"Clear filters\\\" button disappearing. All count updates and no-results states update immediately when criteria changed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After page reload: All valid published jobs and applications persist. Senior Frontend Developer shows 2 original applications (Jan 15 posting), all 5 valid jobs retained. Invalid data properly rejected: Test Job with invalid salary (min $200k > max $100k) not persisted after reload (was shown with success notification but rejected by backend). Duplicate application also not persisted. Job deletion of Senior Backend Developer remains in effect - job not restored after reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Every job card displays: job title (e.g., Senior Backend Developer), company name (TechCorp Solutions), industry badge (Technology), employment type badge (Full-time), location (San Francisco, CA), salary range ($120k - $160k), posting date (Yesterday/Jan dates), and required skills tags (Python, Java, PostgreSQL, etc.).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Job details page displays: title (Senior Backend Developer), company (TechCorp Solutions), industry (Technology), employment type (Full-time), location (San Francisco, CA), salary range ($120k - $160k), posting date (Posted Yesterday), full description (\\\"We are looking for an experienced backend developer...\\\"), and required skills (Python, Java, PostgreSQL). All match the created listing.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"For each application shown under Senior Frontend Developer job, the employer can view: applicant name (Alex Johnson, Maria Garcia), email (alex.j@email.com, maria.g@email.com), optional phone (555-0101, 555-0102), message text, and submission date (Jan 20, Jan 22). Each appears as a distinct record.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Newly submitted application for John Smith shows submission date \\\"Yesterday\\\" which is accurate relative to current date (2026-08-24). New job \\\"Senior Backend Developer\\\" posted shows date \\\"Posted Yesterday\\\" which is also accurate.\"}]}"
